# The PAM stack `cybou-authd` opens, installed as /etc/pam.d/cybou.
#
# It is deliberately the ordinary Unix password check and nothing else. A stack that included
# session or password management would let this service change accounts; it only ever asks whether
# one accepts a secret. `account` is included because an expired or locked account must not
# authenticate, which is what makes `usermod -L` a way to revoke access.

auth     required   pam_unix.so
account  required   pam_unix.so
